Restore Setup_Driver_Names' computer-name table base (dd2h.exe 0x44c550).
At 0x44c5a5 ESI receives the human-driver count; 0x44c5a7 shifts it left
by four, 0x44c5aa subtracts 16 and 0x44c5b3 adds 0x467664. The first
computer name is therefore 0x467654 + humans*16. Each subsequent name
advances another 16 bytes (0x44c5c1), and each destination champ_info
record advances 54 bytes (0x44c5cc).

Ghidra expressed the starting address as &num_races + humans*8 before
assigning it to a WORD pointer. Our byte-typed num_races symbol makes
that initial addition advance only 8 bytes per human; the later WORD
pointer increments still advance 16. With one human this starts at
0x46765c, the num_cars DWORD, then copies truncated/empty suffixes of
the actual names. Live championship Retire/Yes -> View League reproduced
all affected rows; the unmodified original produced the full names and
the same point totals. Use explicit byte address arithmetic for the
original base, keeping the existing WORD-pointer loop stride intact.

